"xw3fcnb03hm4": {
"body": "On February 9, 2026, a frontend routing regression caused the legacy Quay.io UI to become temporarily inaccessible for roughly 45 minutes, though all backend APIs and image pulls remained fully operational. We restored access by deploying a fix to the routing configuration. Moving forward, we are strengthening our deployment procedures by requiring staging validations and integrating automated UI tests into our release pipeline to catch similar regressions before they reach production.",
"first_seen": "2026-09-04T07:06:16Z",
"impact": "critical",
"last_seen": "2026-09-05T05:19:27Z",
"resolved_at": "2026-02-09T22:24:46.685Z",
"resolved_inferred": false,
"started_at": "2026-02-09T21:43:04.948Z",
"state": "postmortem",
"title": "Quay.io UI Could Not Be Loaded",
"updated_at": "2026-06-18T17:42:19.500Z",
"url": "https://stspg.io/6fz9dqh2n56j"
},
"ygxq09yvyx6w": {
"body": "This incident was caused by a database change which was improperly rolled out. Quay engineers were deploying an update which dropped a no longer utilized table, however, this was deployed all at once rather than in phases. That meant that our existing deployment began crashing once the table was dropped, causing API failures since the table was being queried with every request to the API. The SRE team had to manually scale down the old deployment to allow the newer one to progress which restored API functionality. Going forward we are reviewing our process for database migrations and implementing additional checks to ensure that these migrations happen in two steps: application update first and database migrations second.",
"first_seen": "2026-09-04T07:06:16Z",
"impact": "minor",
"last_seen": "2026-09-05T05:19:27Z",
"resolved_at": "2026-02-18T21:40:55.878Z",
"resolved_inferred": false,
"started_at": "2026-02-18T20:51:20.217Z",
"state": "postmortem",
"title": "quay.io intermittent API failures",
"updated_at": "2026-02-26T18:06:57.246Z",
"url": "https://stspg.io/77rnz2tz8992"
},
